{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>An Egyptian man.</b> He was the father of the blasphemer, as it is said (Leviticus 24:10): ״והוא בן איש מצרי״." "<b>Striking a Hebrew man.</b> He was the husband of Shelomit, and the Egyptian set his eye upon her. At night he would rouse him and take him out of his house, and then he himself would return and enter the house and lie with his wife, she thinking he was her husband. And when the husband returned to his home and became aware of the matter, the Egyptian would strike him and subject him to forced labor all day long."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:34.995717124Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}